From: DshanControl contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: align i.MX6ULL Pro touch and eMMC with desktop baseline

The selected panel and the existing Goodix configuration data are 1024x600,
but the input driver's advertised coordinate bounds still say 800x480.
Align those bounds without enabling controller firmware/configuration updates.

Use the conservative USDHC2 settings documented by the BSP's
skills/imx6ull-buildroot-emmc-guide/SKILL.md: four data lines, no 1.8 V
switching and a 50 MHz clock limit. This is a software configuration based on
that reference, not new physical validation of this DshanControl image.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6ull-14x14-evk.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6ull-14x14-evk.dts
@@ -302,8 +302,8 @@
                 irq-flags = <2>;                /*1:rising 2: falling*/
 
                 touchscreen-max-id = <5>;
-                touchscreen-size-x = <800>;
-                touchscreen-size-y = <480>;
+                touchscreen-size-x = <1024>;
+                touchscreen-size-y = <600>;
                 touchscreen-max-w = <1024>;
                 touchscreen-max-p = <1024>;
                 /*touchscreen-key-map = <172>, <158>;*/ /*KEY_HOMEPAGE, KEY_BACK*/
@@ -886,8 +886,10 @@
 
 &usdhc2 {
         pinctrl-names = "default";
-        pinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_usdhc2_8bit>;
-        bus-width = <8>;
+        pinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_usdhc2>;
+        bus-width = <4>;
+        no-1-8-v;
+        max-frequency = <50000000>;
         non-removable;
         status = "okay";
 };
